libc++'s locales on Kosmos (docs/gpu3d.md G2, for the Vulkan CTS; Diego,
19 November 2026: localization on). libc++ chooses how to reach the C
library's locales by the platform's macros, and Kosmos's triple names
none, so it fell to the fallback written for z/OS, which defines a
vasprintf of its own over the one Kosmos's <stdio.h> declares. Kosmos has
one locale, "C", which the POSIX layer's newlocale hands out - LLVM's own
libc's case exactly - so `__kosmos__` (runtime/cxx/kosmos.cmake) gets a
support header of that shape: newlocale, freelocale, setlocale and
localeconv from the C library, and libc++'s own no_locale shims for the
rest, each the plain C function. The header is listed where libc++ lists
its headers, to be installed and in its module map; and Kosmos joins the
platforms libc++ gives its default character table, as llvm-libc does,
since there is no locale's table to read.

